ronger on stress resilience, D stronger on attention and responsibility. Both have cooperation concerns. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is essential. Both have serious issues. Which is more likely to be mitigated? Hard to say. The panel may need to decide.\n\nGiven we are agent_2, we can either maintain vote for B, but we need to address the concerns raised by others. We can argue that B's stress handling and reliability outweigh his interpersonal issues, which can be mitigated with training, whereas D's hot temper may be more dangerous under stress. Also D's \"adequate\" response to unexpected events is less strong than B's \"handles stress very well\". So we could keep B.\n\nThus we will respond: I understand the points about D, but I remain convinced B is best because of his strong reliability and stress resilience, and his technical competence, while his interpersonal issues are concerning but can be addressed. Also note B's weak memory for numbers is a concern but may be mitigated with tools. So we keep vote B.\n\nWe need to reference specific facts: B \"very conscientious\", \"handles stress very well\", \"good at assessing weather conditions\", \"excellent computer skills\". Also note concerns: \"weak memory for numbers\", \"makes nasty remarks\", \"can be uncooperative\". Compare to D's \"takes responsibility seriously\", \"solves problems extremely well\", \"concentrates very well\", \"responds adequately to unexpected events\", \"hot temper\", \"know-it-all\". Argue that B's stress handling is more critical for long-haul, and his reliability is higher. So we keep B.\n\nThus public message: I am less convinced by D's profile, maintain B. Provide reasoning.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
